      "line_end": 35,
      "title": "SQL query built from the name query parameter",
      "description": "Search interpolates the name query parameter directly into the SQL text with Sprintf. Nothing escapes or validates the value before QueryContext runs it. Any caller of GET /users can inject SQL and read or alter every table in the database. Pass the name as a bound parameter to QueryContext instead of formatting it into the string.",
      "suggested_change": "rows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search interpolates the name query parameter directly into the SQL text with Sprintf. Nothing escapes or validates the value before QueryContext runs it.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of GET /users can inject SQL and read or alter every table in the database.",
      "fix": "Pass the name as a bound parameter to QueryContext instead of formatting it into the string."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
      "severity": "critical",
      "category": "bug",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "file_path": "internal/api/handler.go",
      "line_number": 61,
      "line_end": 64,
      "title": "Mutex stays locked on the missing-key return",
      "description": "Count locks h.mu on line 60 and then returns on line 63 without unlocking when key is empty. The only Unlock sits on line 67, after that return. One request to GET /count without a key leaves the mutex held forever. Every later Count request blocks on Lock and the endpoint hangs. Validate key before taking the lock, or use defer h.mu.Unlock() right after Lock.",
      "suggested_change": "if key == \"\" {\n\t\thttp.Error(w, \"missing key\", http.StatusBadRequest)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\th.mu.Lock()",
      "source": "semgrep:trailofbits.go.missing-unlock-before-return.missing-unlock-before-return",
      "candidate": "c2",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Count locks h.mu on line 60 and then returns on line 63 without unlocking when key is empty. The only Unlock sits on line 67, after that return.",
      "consequence": "One request to GET /count without a key leaves the mutex held forever. Every later Count request blocks on Lock and the endpoint hangs.",
      "fix": "Validate key before taking the lock, or use defer h.mu.Unlock() right after Lock."
    },
