      "line_end": 84,
      "title": "Body closed before the error check in fetchStatus",
      "description": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close() on line 83 before checking err on line 84. When http.Get fails, resp is nil and the deferred call dereferences a nil pointer. Any upstream failure panics the handler goroutine, so GET /upstream drops the connection instead of returning 502. The error branch in Upstream never runs. Check err first and only defer the Close after the error check.",
      "suggested_change": "resp, err := http.Get(url)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn 0, err\n\t}\n\tdefer resp.Body.Close()",
      "source": null,
      "candidate": null,
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "fetchStatus defers resp.Body.Close() on line 83 before checking err on line 84. When http.Get fails, resp is nil and the deferred call dereferences a nil pointer.",
      "consequence": "Any upstream failure panics the handler goroutine, so GET /upstream drops the connection instead of returning 502. The error branch in Upstream never runs.",
      "fix": "Check err first and only defer the Close after the error check."
    },
