      "title": "Row iteration error ignored in Search",
      "description": "Search never calls rows.Err() after the rows.Next() loop ends. A connection or driver error during iteration ends the loop silently. Clients receive a 200 response with a truncated user list when the database fails mid-query. Check rows.Err() after the loop and answer with a 500 when it is set.",
      "suggested_change": "if err := rows.Err(); err != nil {\n\t\thttp.Error(w, \"search failed\", http.StatusInternalServerError)\n\t\treturn\n\t}\n\t_ = json.NewEncoder(w).Encode(users)",
      "source": null,
